<p class="eyebrow">Independent case study · Notion public-site baseline</p><h1>SEO/AEO/GEO Optimization Case Study</h1>
<p>This independent study uses Notion as a real B2B SaaS research subject. It is not client work and is not affiliated with Notion.</p>
<h2>Research question</h2><p>Which page, entity and evidence signals make a brand easier to retrieve, summarize, cite and compare — and where does a conventional SEO audit fail to capture those signals?</p>
<h2>Baseline v1</h2><p>The public site gives us unusually clear evidence to test: explicit workspace positioning, project-management capabilities, AI agents, enterprise search, connector coverage and structured pricing. That makes it suitable for testing different intent families rather than reducing visibility to one score.</p>
<div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Discovery</h3><p>Can the brand surface for category-level workspace and project-management questions?</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Comparison</h3><p>Can systems retrieve enough explicit evidence to compare capabilities and trade-offs?</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Pricing & value</h3><p>Are plan boundaries and AI packaging answerable without inference?</p></article><article class="card"><h3>AI capabilities</h3><p>Can agents, enterprise search and connected-app capabilities be retrieved accurately?</p></article></div>
<h2>Prompt dataset</h2><p>Baseline v1 contains 12 controlled prompts across category discovery, alternatives, comparisons, capabilities, pricing/value, implementation and recommendation intent. Raw prompt definitions are versioned in the repository before observations are scored.</p>
<h2>Evidence standard</h2><p>Observed public evidence, interpretation and proposed intervention are reported separately. No traffic, ranking, citation or revenue improvement is claimed unless it can be measured after an intervention.</p>
<h2>Next measurement layer</h2><p>Each observation will record prompt family, brand mention, citation presence, recommendation inclusion, source URL and notes. Python aggregation is already versioned, but it deliberately refuses to produce results until real observations exist.</p>
</Base>